Do not place the actual secret in source, documentation, workflow state, issue text, test output, or examples.

## Security model

The overall workflow needs GitHub publication authority, but the worker does not.

The worker produces candidate work and local commits. The trusted runtime independently validates the result, publishes the exact approved SHA, and creates/reconciles the draft PR. Giving publication credentials to the worker would bypass that trusted boundary and create a confused-deputy and privilege-escalation path.

