- Validate transform-to-transform dependencies with a deterministic graph traversal and report a concrete cycle path.
- Resolve transforms through an indexed ready queue so each dependency edge is processed once and plugin discovery begins only after all inputs are ready.
- Preserve the legacy queue's evaluation order and generated action names for existing valid configurations.
- Retain the intentional single-transform and terminal empty-input compatibility fallbacks, while failing ambiguous unresolved graphs.
- Add runtime parser, graph validation, and connect dry-run coverage for cycles, self-cycles, partial inputs, duplicate inputs, reverse-declared chains, fallback compatibility, and action-index boundaries.

