- retained scenario identity/version;
- exact trader identity/version;
- exact strategy/decision-policy identity where applicable;
- explicit starting state and capital/risk envelope;
- normal and adversarial market conditions;
- execution/error/disconnect scenarios;
- slippage/spread/latency/staleness scenarios where relevant;
- drawdown and loss-control scenarios;
- position/risk-limit scenarios;
- reconciliation and degraded-mode scenarios;
- complete retained evidence of actions, decisions, outcomes and violations.

The Laboratory must not possess real-capital trading authority.

## 2. CIBO role

CIBO acts as trainer, evaluator and decision-intelligence supervisor inside the Laboratory and later as a governed executive/trader-management intelligence component in DEMO and any separately authorized bounded live scope.

CIBO may:
- introduce traders to their governed objective and operating contract;
- teach market/instrument/risk context;
- assign scenarios and exercises;
- explain failures;
- require remediation/retraining;
- generate structured evaluations and evidence;
- recommend promotion to the next certification stage;
- consume certified market/economic/risk evidence;
