Issue #32674: [Detail Bug] Glossary: left panel shows stale glossary displayName after displayName-only edit

# Detail Bug Report

https://app.detail.dev/org_3377c26d-da48-4ccd-b83a-22c542f4fe83/bugs/bug_a3f103f7-5384-406e-98dd-95a38dde1592

Introduced in [#16066](https://github.com/open-metadata/OpenMetadata/pull/16066) by @chirag-madlani on Apr 30, 2024

# Summary
- **Context**: The `GlossaryLeftPanel` component renders the left-hand side menu of glossary names in the Glossary page; each menu item's label comes from a `useMemo` that builds antd `Menu` items from the `glossaries` prop, memoized on the `glossaries` array reference.
- **Bug**: When a glossary's `displayName` is edited through the normal edit flow (without renaming the `name`/FQN), the left panel menu still shows the stale `displayName`, while the rest of the Glossary UI (header, active-glossary-driven content) shows the new one.
- **Actual vs. expected**: After a successful glossary `displayName` edit, the right-hand glossary header / page title (`getEntityName(activeGlossary)`) shows the new `displayName`, but the left panel menu item label keeps displaying the old `displayName`.
- **Impact**: Within a single Glossary page session, a `displayName`-only edit leaves the menu stale until a user action that replaces the `glossaries` array reference (rename of `name`/FQN, glossary delete, glossary-term creation, load-more pagination, or leaving and re-entering the page).

# Code with Bug
`openmetadata-ui/src/main/resources/ui/src/components/Glossary/useGlossary.store.ts`
```ts
if (index !== -1) {
  glossaries[index] = updatedGlossary; // <-- BUG 🔴 mutates array in place; glossaries ref unchanged so memoized menu labels don't update
}
```

`openmetadata-ui/src/main/resources/ui/src/pages/Glossary/GlossaryLeftPanel/GlossaryLeftPanel.component.tsx`
```tsx
const menuItems: ItemType[] = useMemo(() => {
  return glossaries.reduce((acc, glossary) => {
    return [
      ...acc,
      {
        key: glossary.fullyQualifiedName ?? '',
        label: getEntityName(glossary),
        icon: <GlossaryIcon height={16} width={16} />,
      },
    ];
  }, [] as ItemType[]);
}, [glossaries]); // <-- BUG 🔴 depends only on array reference; in-place store mutation is invisible
```

`openmetadata-ui/src/main/resources/ui/src/pages/Glossary/GlossaryPage/GlossaryPage.component.tsx`
```tsx
updateActiveGlossary({ ...updatedData, ...response });

if (activeGlossary?.name !== updatedData.name) { // <-- BUG 🔴 displayName-only edits skip fetchGlossaryList, so list ref never refreshed
  navigate(getGlossaryPath(response.fullyQualifiedName));
  fetchGlossaryList();
}
```

# Explanation
- `GlossaryLeftPanel` memoizes its menu items and only recomputes when the `glossaries` prop reference changes.
- On a `displayName`-only edit, `GlossaryPage.updateGlossary` updates the store via `updateActiveGlossary` but intentionally does not refresh the glossary list (`fetchGlossaryList`) because `name` is unchanged.
- `useGlossaryStore.updateActiveGlossary` updates `activeGlossary` but mutates the `glossaries` array in place (`glossaries[index] = updatedGlossary`), preserving the array reference. As a result, `GlossaryLeftPanel` does not recompute its memoized menu labels and continues showing the old `displayName`.

## Codebase Inconsistency
`updateGlossary` (same store) updates the list immutably (fresh array reference), but `updateActiveGlossary` does not:

`openmetadata-ui/src/main/resources/ui/src/components/Glossary/useGlossary.store.ts`
```ts
set({
  glossaries: glossaries.map((g, index) =>
    index === glossaryIndex ? updatedGlossary : g
  ),
});
```

# Failing Test
`openmetadata-ui/src/main/resources/ui/src/pages/Glossary/GlossaryPage/GlossaryLeftPanel.integration.test.tsx`

Test demonstrates real behavior with the real Zustand store + real `GlossaryPage` + real `GlossaryLeftPanel` (only network mocked): after patching a glossary with `displayName: 'Alpha Renamed'` (name unchanged), the active glossary displayName updates but the left menu still shows `Alpha`.

Test output:
```
PASS @openmetadata src/pages/Glossary/GlossaryPage/GlossaryLeftPanel.integration.test.tsx
  GlossaryPage + real store + real GlossaryLeftPanel
    ✓ left panel shows stale displayName after a displayName-only edit (178 ms)
```

# Recommended Fix
Make `useGlossaryStore.updateActiveGlossary` update `glossaries` immutably (create a new array reference) instead of mutating in place, mirroring the existing `updateGlossary` pattern:

`openmetadata-ui/src/main/resources/ui/src/components/Glossary/useGlossary.store.ts`
```ts
if (index !== -1) {
  set({ // create a new array reference so downstream memos observe the change
    glossaries: glossaries.map((g, i) => (i === index ? updatedGlossary : g)),
  });
}
```

# History
This bug was introduced in commit 0701fed67e. PR #16066 "Glossary expand fix" (2024-04-30) moved glossary updates to a Zustand `activeGlossary` model and gated `fetchGlossaryList` on `name` changes; for `displayName`-only edits there was no longer a path that replaced the `glossaries` array reference, so the left panel menu became stale. A later change (#16372) attempted to sync the list by mutating `glossaries[index]` in place, but this still does not change the array reference so the memoized menu remains stale.

