- held-out task utility with confidence intervals;
- labeled calibration examples / seconds / trials;
- unlabeled adaptation examples / seconds;
- cross-session and cross-subject transfer;
- untouched final-assessment score.

Robustness:

- montage/channel drop and reorder;
- sampling-rate/preprocessing perturbations where scientifically meaningful;
- artifact sensitivity;
- session/device/domain shift when datasets permit;
- seed/split sensitivity;
- failure rate and missing-result preservation.

Model/evidence:

- exact dataset/entity lineage;
- pretraining overlap verdict;
- preprocessing/calibration/adaptation authority;
- exact promoted model artifact identity;
- score/probability/uncertainty semantics;
- representation geometry/domain leakage separate from task utility;
