## Source-level root cause already established

At current HEAD, `GlobalController.process_completed_tasks()` does:

```text
with result_list_lock:
    iterate result_queue
    -> finalize_execution_group(group)
```

`finalize_execution_group()` can synchronously call:

```text
agent.reflect(group.task, detail)
-> BaseAgent.reflect()
-> llm.few_shot_generate_thoughts(...)
```

and then performs task-status / feedback post-processing.

Thus `result_list_lock` is held across model/network/file/task-manager work.

`BaseAgent.reflect()` has no controller shutdown/cancellation parameter. The OpenAI-compatible model wrapper itself has a finite provider wall-clock budget (`DEFAULT_OPENAI_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=120s`), while `GlobalController.shutdown_grace_period` is `5s`. Therefore merely waiting for the model wrapper's normal timeout is incompatible with bounded controller shutdown.

